PrivateWiki

You control the "openess" or "closeness" of your wiki. This is specially important when the name of your wiki is not a secret.

You also control who can see what. See HelpPublicPages

To change now the openess of your wiki, click on DoOpenWiki, DoMentorWiki or DoClosedWiki. Don't lock yourself out, see below.


DoOpenWiki
  PrivateOpenWiki -- very open wikis

  In "very open" wikis, changes from both guests and members are "drafts" only if sent this way by the author, or else the changes are permanent.

  Beware: this means that *anybody* can change *anything* in "very open" wikis!


DoMentorWiki
  PrivateMentorWiki -- open wikis 

  "open" wikis require mentor approval to validate new members and changes to pages by guests. This is the "normal" set up.

  Don't lock yourself out! Remember to register yourself as a mentor before closing the door. See SimpliWikiDoc


DoClosedWiki
  PrivateClosedWiki -- very closed wikis 

  On such wikis, guests can mainly visit "Public" and "Guest" pages only, ie regular pages can be visited by members of the wiki only

-----

This page may contain some additional "directives" about your wiki. Valid content (all optional):

Openness:
- open: false for very closed wikis only
- veryOpen: true or false
- mentors: @abc @efg -- list mentors

Look:
- rows: less rows means bigger characters, try 20
- cols: number of columns, default is 50
- lang: either "en" or "fr" (english or french)
- title: turn Anonymous into a nice title
- fetch: lists "custom" pages, see HelpPrefetch
- cssStyle: css page or url, see CssStyles

